But we do have a couple
of questions to start.

00:46:34.030 --> 00:46:39.233
So if you guys maybe wanna
take the first couple?

00:46:39.233 --> 00:46:43.738
&gt;&gt; So first question is, what career skill
sets, education, training should we be

00:46:43.738 --> 00:46:48.320
focusing on now in the future for
visual computing in a workplace?

00:46:48.320 --> 00:46:52.140
One thing I wanna mention with graphics
and visual computing in general is that

00:46:52.140 --> 00:46:55.860
people usually think of visual computing
as complementary to something else.

00:46:55.860 --> 00:47:00.720
So you should take a bunch of

00:47:00.720 --> 00:47:04.680
visual computing courses, take the ones
in certificate, that's why George and

00:47:04.680 --> 00:47:07.090
I picked those,
is they give you a good basis.

00:47:07.090 --> 00:47:08.890
But we always want people
to have something else.

00:47:08.890 --> 00:47:11.710
And so, I talked about all the machine
learning and the data science and

00:47:11.710 --> 00:47:12.900
that sort of thing.

00:47:12.900 --> 00:47:16.470
It would be a nice thing to
mix a lot of this with that.

00:47:16.470 --> 00:47:20.747
People also mix visual computing with
human computer interaction, HDI classes.

00:47:20.747 --> 00:47:24.640
Where the hackers will mix visual
computing with systems type classes.

00:47:24.640 --> 00:47:26.090
Graphics, just one of those things and

00:47:26.090 --> 00:47:28.520
visual computing in general
is one of those things.

00:47:28.520 --> 00:47:33.620
Where it's nice to mix them in
a hybrid way with other areas.

00:47:33.620 --> 00:47:37.150
And so almost everyone who comes
to me says they wanna do graphics,

00:47:37.150 --> 00:47:40.610
then what they wanna do it for, I always
tell them to add something else to it.

00:47:40.610 --> 00:47:43.640
It's always typically the visual
certificate is the core.

00:47:43.640 --> 00:47:45.710
But ask yourself, do I care about systems?

00:47:45.710 --> 00:47:47.262
Do I care about HDI?

00:47:47.262 --> 00:47:49.400
Do I care about hard works.

00:47:49.400 --> 00:47:51.240
People make graphics cards,
that's part of graphics.

00:47:51.240 --> 00:47:53.153
So architecture or something.

00:47:53.153 --> 00:47:57.276
But find the other thing and once you
know the two things that you want, visual

00:47:57.276 --> 00:48:01.050
computing plus Whatever the other thing
is, it will guide you through the visual

00:48:01.050 --> 00:48:04.105
computing courses to choose the ones that
are most appropriate than hybridization.

00:48:04.105 --> 00:48:06.053
Computational geometry, math.

00:48:06.053 --> 00:48:08.890
Leo Guibas proves a bunch
of theorems all the time.

00:48:08.890 --> 00:48:11.375
So if you take his classes,
you can get more into mathematics.

00:48:11.375 --> 00:48:16.287
But that's my advice, is to always find
the other field you want in addition

00:48:16.287 --> 00:48:18.994
to visual computing and hybridize them.

00:48:18.994 --> 00:48:24.976
&gt;&gt; Okay, so the second question is,
will the technology improve better and

00:48:24.976 --> 00:48:31.452
more accurate medical research after
this like cancer, diabetes and others?

00:48:31.452 --> 00:48:35.330
&gt;&gt; So that's an interesting question.

00:48:35.330 --> 00:48:42.560
Visual computing isn't necessarily linked
directly to research and medical imaging.

00:48:42.560 --> 00:48:46.590
However, a lot of the techniques
that we're talking about in sensing,

00:48:46.590 --> 00:48:49.580
in computational imaging, and
the applied mathematics and

00:48:49.580 --> 00:48:54.520
imagery construction are also
being used in medical imaging.

00:48:54.520 --> 00:48:59.270
We work very closely with faculties
